<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sadr</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sadr was a title of high office in the Safavid state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. In Safavid practice the sadr was closely associated with supervising the religious establishment and pious endowments, and accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> also mention the title alongside that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vakil">vakil</a> in describing the senior official who managed civil affairs. The office reflected the close connection between state administration and Shia religious authority in Safavid Iran.</p></div>
